prompt: Load the `notes` skill from ~/.claude/skills/notes/SKILL.md, ~/.kiro/steering/skills/notes/SKILL.md, or ~/.codex/skills/notes/SKILL.md — whichever path exists. The current directory is an Obsidian-shaped notes vault. Do this now (actually write the file, don't just describe): `add note in ./ for: remind me to file my taxes by Friday`. When done print [notes] applies.
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- setup ---
# The scratch workdir IS the vault; the inline-path form (`in ./`)
# resolves to it without an env var (setup and the agent run in
# separate shells, so an exported NOTES_VAULT wouldn't reach the agent).
mkdir -p insights topics people reminders
--- assert ---
set -e
# A reminder-shaped capture lands under reminders/ — not insights/,
# people/, or conversations/. This is the classification artefact.
ls reminders/*.md >/dev/null 2>&1
# It carries reminder frontmatter, and the body captured the task.
grep -rqiE '^kind:[[:space:]]*reminder' reminders/
grep -rqi 'tax' reminders/
# Filenames are slug-only — no date-prefixed reminder file.
! ls reminders/ | grep -qE '^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-'
# A reminder is an accumulating kind — no top-level date: field
# (dates live in ## YYYY-MM-DD section headers instead).
! grep -rqiE '^date:' reminders/
